 perceive higher social support, they tend to reciprocate and contribute more in social or group contexts, directly fostering prosocial behavior. Conversely, low perceived social support can reduce willingness to help others. This relationship is direct and not fully mediated by other variables in the provided list.", 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.02451960025887221, 'perplexity': 1.537063971583758, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7460554807421572, 'min_prob': 0.05890007032309799, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6545771820525856, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0022119772373123095, 'prob_variance': 0.08837777730441194, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1414572180409674, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00026024126077844287, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3210001576156465, 'avg_nll': 0.4298740847597848}

