106. Depressive symptoms (IDS-SR)-[POSITIVE]->Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6)
   Properties: {'session_id': '97aa030b-2a66-4fd5-a273-ad76ab75dfee', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8194199761303147, 'citations': ['https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/ejn.15992', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165178120332297', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-85514-0', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2023.1130989/full'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.1075211357639815, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Step 1: The explanation posits that depressive symptoms lead to increased social withdrawal and reduced interpersonal contact. This is a reasonable behavioral link, as depressive symptoms are often associated with social withdrawal.  \\nStep 2: The explanation claims that reduced interpersonal contact results in lower exposure to pathogens. This is plausible\\u2014reduced social interaction could limit exposure to communicable diseases.  \\nStep 3: The key causal step is that lower pathogen exposure causes the immune system to increase baseline proinflammatory cytokines (TNF-alpha and IL-6) as a compensatory mechanism to maintain immune vigilance. This step is speculative and not well-supported by common immunological principles. Typically, decreased microbial stimulation tends to downregulate, not upregulate, immune activation; the hygiene hypothesis, for instance, suggests that lack of microbial exposure can dysregulate immunity (e.g., allergies, autoimmunity), but not straightforwardly increase proinflammatory cytokines as a compensatory baseline.  \\nStep 4: The explanation concludes that behavioral isolation from depression directly causes heightened proinflammatory processes via this compensatory immune mechanism. This is an internally coherent narrative but relies on a questionable biological premise in step 3."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', '