, 'original_motivation': 'Depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) cause proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) to increase via neuroimmune mechanisms. Higher levels of depressive symptoms can directly upregulate inflammatory cytokines, leading to increased TNF-alpha and IL-6. Conversely, reducing depressive symptoms can lower these proinflammatory markers. This is a direct, positive causal relationship.', 'prob_std': 0.26592309597561165, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.3181560239014132, 'max_window_entropy': 1.1094551686408467}

