ive for restorative sleep and disrupts circadian rhythms, leading to greater sleep disturbance. Conversely, increased physical activity tends to improve sleep quality and duration. This relationship is supported by evidence that physical activity interventions can reduce sleep problems.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.004049013077523958, 'perplexity': 1.5088491385409801, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7721180609172157, 'min_prob': 0.009280285421088228, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6373402903568782, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004937188701930046, 'prob_variance': 0.08787271325412985, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1999636505241429, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0011648972326727728, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3323538025936119, 'avg_nll': 0.41134720032867483}

