208. Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10)-[NEGATIVE]->Depressive symptoms (IDS-SR)
   Properties: {'session_id': '97aa030b-2a66-4fd5-a273-ad76ab75dfee', 'judge_perplexity': 428819237070435.2, 'citations': ['https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2023.1130989/full', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12024626/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0929510023444804, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Step 1: The explanation presents a negative causal relationship: increased anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) reduce depressive symptoms.  \\nStep 2: The mechanism claimed is that IL-10 suppresses the production of neurotransmitters such as serotonin and dopamine.  \\nStep 3: The explanation further claims that these neurotransmitters are \\"thought to be elevated in depression,\\" and that curtailing their synthesis improves mood and reduces depressive symptoms.  \\nStep 4: This chain of reasoning assumes that reducing serotonin and dopamine is beneficial for mood, and that their elevation is associated with depression.  \\nStep 5: The logic is internally inconsistent. The widely accepted (scientifically and logically) view is that decreased, not increased, levels of serotonin and dopamine are associated with depressive symptoms. Thus, suppressing their production would not logically lead to improved mood or reduced depressive symptoms.  \\nStep 6: The explanation\'s internal logic is flawed because the mechanism contradicts the claimed outcome. If IL-10 reduces neurotransmitter levels, and if those neurotransmitters are beneficial for mood, then IL-10 should worsen, not improve, depressive symptoms according to the logic presented.  \\nStep 7: Even without external knowledge, the explanation is self-contradictory: it claims reducing neurotransmitters improves mood, while also implying that more neurotransmitters are bad for mood, which does not cohere logically."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.8108565835497068, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6501213389683851, 'motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) causally reduce depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) by directly suppressing the production of neurotransmitters such as serotonin and dopamine, which are thought to be elevated in depression. By increasing IL-10 levels, the excessive synthesis of these neurotransmitters is curtailed, leading to improved mood and fewer depressive symptoms. Conversely, when anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) are reduced, unchecked neurotransmitter production exacerbates depressive symptoms (IDS-SR).', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) causally reduce depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) by directly suppressing the production of neurotransmitters such as serotonin and dopamine, which are thought to be elevated in depression. By increasing IL-10 levels, the excessive synthesis of these neurotransmitters is curtailed, leading to improved mood and fewer depressive symptoms. Conversely, when anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) are reduced, unchecked neurotransmitter production exacerbates depressive symptoms (IDS-SR).', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8697218141277773, 'min_prob': 0.03930435640882725, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7359542439644959, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0023381024259483633, 'prob_variance': 0.05160619473480511, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.000489847764237504, 'judge_prob_std': 0.30487866823456244, 'avg_nll': 0.2132881448968271, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3725799714646802, 'original_motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) causally reduce depressive symptoms (IDS-SR). Higher levels of IL-10, an anti-inflammatory cytokine, decrease neuroinflammation, which is implicated in the pathophysiology of depression. Therefore, increasing IL-10 leads to fewer depressive symptoms, while decreasing IL-10 may allow depressive symptoms to increase.', 'prob_std': 0.22716996882247686, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.2377412486896686, 'max_window_entropy': 0.6812851691080738}

