   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1411363609476497, 'original_motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) causes anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to decrease. Chronic rumination increases psychological stress, which can suppress anti-inflammatory cytokines like IL-10 via neuroendocrine and immune pathways. Therefore, an increase in rumination causally leads to a decrease in anti-inflammatory processes.', 'session_id': '9329f27d-8aa4-4019-ac78-6201736096e8', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6784177646016891, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0950499443352679, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a temporally coherent and internally consistent account (meeting TEMPORALITY and COHERENCE) by stating that rumination precedes and influences IL-10 production without contradiction or circularity. However, it lacks a specific and plausible causal mechanism (failing PLAUSIBILITY), as it only vaguely suggests that \\"focused attention on emotional experiences\\" enhances immune regulation without detailing how this occurs biologically. The STRENGTH of the relationship is also not clearly conveyed; the explanation offers no indication of the relative importance or significance of rumination\'s effect on anti-inflammatory processes."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6761376073456314, 'motivation': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves focused attention on emotional experiences, which can actually enhance the regulation of the immune system. By repeatedly thinking about stressors, individuals may stimulate pathways that increase the production of anti-inflammatory cytokines like IL-10, thereby promoting anti-inflammatory processes.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'R